      en: "Then the elder Subhūti rose from his seat among the assembly, bared his right shoulder, knelt on his right knee, joined his palms in reverence, and said to the Buddha: How rare, World-Honored One! The Tathāgata watches over and cares for all bodhisattvas, and entrusts all bodhisattvas well. World-Honored One, when good men and good women set their minds on supreme perfect awakening, how should they abide, and how should they subdue their minds? The Buddha said: Excellent, excellent, Subhūti! It is as you say — the Tathāgata watches over and entrusts the bodhisattvas well. Listen closely now, and I shall tell you: good men and good women who set their minds on supreme perfect awakening should abide thus, and subdue their minds thus. Yes indeed, World-Honored One, we wish and are glad to hear it."
